{% doc %}
  Prints the handle of the category a product belongs to — nothing when it has
  none. Used by the breadcrumb and by the cross-sell strip, which must agree.

  Collection handles are translated per market: `oak` is served as
  `chene-massif` in French, `bamboo` as `bambou`. A deny-list of English
  handles therefore matches nothing outside English, and the material or
  catch-all collections quietly pose as the category — which is how French
  breadcrumbs came to read "Accueil / Chêne massif". The seven categories are
  instead marked once in the admin with `custom.is_category`, a value that is
  the same in every language.

  Prefers the collection the visitor arrived through, when that one is a
  category, so the breadcrumb reflects the path actually taken.

  Prints a handle, because a snippet cannot hand a variable back to its caller.
  Capture it, then look the collection up:

  @param {object} product - The product to resolve a category for

  @example
  {% capture parent_handle %}{% render 'parent-collection', product: product %}{% endcapture %}
  {% assign parent = collections[parent_handle] %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign found = ''

  if collection.metafields.custom.is_category
    assign found = collection.handle
  endif

  if found == blank
    for c in product.collections
      if c.metafields.custom.is_category
        assign found = c.handle
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  echo found | strip
-%}
